B.bbB=new A.R("Choose who marches off.",B.C)
B.bbC=new A.R("","The Danes and the Norwegians start at war with every other realm, with war-fleets already on the coast.")
B.bbE=new A.R("The coalition:"," from turn 6, if you come close to victory, the other realms make peace among themselves and all go to war with you until you fall back. The panel at the top left says when; on Hard it comes sooner. It can turn on a runaway rival too.")
B.bbF=new A.R("","Attacking or pillaging a realm you are not at war with declares war \u2014 but not while a peace still holds.")
B.bbI=new A.R("","Then they pay 50% more tax and give more men, and your armies fight 10% harder among them.")
B.bbJ=new A.R("Pillage"," a province your army stands in or borders: not your own, not one guarded by another realm's army, and only if your men outnumber its levies, who fight back.")
B.bbL=new A.R("Light raid, heavy raid or full pillage:"," the harder you strike, the more gold and the more ruin. It takes the army's whole turn, and starts a war if you were not at war.")
B.bbO=new A.R("Danegeld:"," when the Danes are much stronger than you and their hosts stand at your border, they demand half your treasury (at least 100 gold) for 8 turns of peace. It only buys time: when the peace runs out, they come back. East Anglia, the land they came for, is never offered terms. Playing the Danes, you can demand Danegeld yourself.")
B.bbS=new A.R("Attacks are orders"," fought when you end the turn. Each army fights one battle a turn, and armies sent against the same province fight as one host. A realm's province with no army in it is still defended by the levies it musters.")
B.bbU=new A.R("","Playing Scotland, you start with a 6-turn truce with the Norwegians.")
B.bbY=new A.R("Recruit more troops",!1)
B.bbZ=new A.R("YOUR TRIBUTARY",B.k)
B.bc_=new A.R("When turn 8 ends,"," the Danes' Great Heathen Army lands on East Anglia's coast \u2014 the kingdom they come to take (anywhere on England's east coast when you play East Anglia).")
B.bc0=new A.R("A scattered start"," (chosen when you pick your realm) gives every realm one random province with a Barracks and a small host; the rest is independent. Only the conquest goal counts, and no great Viking host lands.")
B.bc1=new A.R("Tap an army"," to select it. Green provinces are ones it can march into \u2014 your own or an ally's. Red ones marked with crossed swords can be attacked.")
B.bc2=new A.R(null,"They refuse.")
B.bc4=new A.R("Gold"," comes from taxes \u2014 the more people, the more gold \u2014 and from markets, ports and mines. Manpower comes from your people, and more from barracks.")
B.bc5=new A.R("Rule 45 provinces."," Every realm wins this way.")
B.bc9=new A.R("","Your armies join only when one marches onto another, or when you press Combine.")
B.bca=new A.R("Submission:"," a realm you have beaten \u2014 down to its last province, with part of its homeland in your hands and an army of yours at its door \u2014 offers to submit. Accept, and its land, armies and treasury join your realm.")
B.bcb=new A.R("2 moves a turn:"," march twice, or march and then attack. Marching into highland takes both moves.")
B.bcd=new A.R(null,"No active game")
B.bcg=new A.R("","Now and then an event card asks you to choose.")
B.bci=new A.R("","The handshake button at the top right opens the realms of Britain.")
B.bcj=new A.R("Both keep the morale, veterancy and moves left.",B.C)
