B.bcw=new A.R("Walls:"," assault a fortified province (its defenders fight 30% harder per wall level), or besiege it \u2014 it falls in a few turns if your army stays beside it. Besieging a realm you are at peace with is war.")
B.bcx=new A.R("When you are attacked,"," SALLY OUT is your charge, and ABANDON gives up the province to save your men: its levies fall back to a neighbouring province you hold.")
B.bcz=new A.R("","You lose if another realm wins first, or if you lose all your land and armies. The panel at the top left shows how far you have come and the rival closest to winning.")
B.bcB=new A.R("","Each turn is one season, four to a year, starting in spring 793.")
B.bcC=new A.R("AT PEACE",B.C)
B.bcE=new A.R("","Your starting provinces also build on their own, with part of your spare gold.")
B.aHw=new A.R(null,B.h)
B.bcF=new A.R(B.m1,B.m0)
B.bcG=new A.R("Every realm can sail."," A host with ships, on the coast and not yet moved this turn, can sail to a coast within reach and march, attack or pillage there. The voyage takes its whole turn. One ship is enough, and a beaten host with ships that has nowhere to fall back to on land escapes by sea.")
B.bcJ=new A.R("Only the army with ships can sail.",B.d4)
B.bcM=new A.R("Leave at least one man behind.",B.V)
B.bcN=new A.R("Battles are live."," Troops and morale fall round by round. CHARGE! is a gamble: it can break a wavering enemy, but against a strong, steady line many of your men fall. Pulling back is free before the lines meet (CALL OFF) and costly after (RETREAT). A side whose morale reaches zero breaks and is cut down.")
